                    s9_fb_ok: `<b>Correct.</b> At €380M revenue with 12 analysts and SOX-defensible reporting, the full stack pays back its complexity tax. The honest rule scales with the firm: a €5M boutique runs (c); a €50M firm considers (c) or (d); only above ~€100M does the full modern stack make sense. Helio Verde is comfortably in <b>(d)+(e)</b> territory. Vendor inertia in this market pushes everyone toward maximum-tool stacks; the analyst's job is to know when that inertia serves them.`,
